  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Marathon Petroleum reported $503M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date across 140 awards, with an average award size of $3.6M and year-over-year change down 7.2%. Marathon Petroleum moved from $11.9M in obligations in FY21 to $93.1M in FY22, then to $359M in FY23, $288M in FY24, and $542M in FY25 before reaching $503M in FY26 to date. Marathon Petroleum shows growth concentrated in FY23 and FY25, with FY26 to date below FY25. Marathon Petroleum’s current totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. Marathon Petroleum’s award count and average award size indicate a mix of mid-size contracts rather than many small awards or a few very large awards. Marathon Petroleum’s year-over-year change down 7.2% signals a decline in obligations compared with the prior comparable period. Marathon Petroleum’s historical fiscal-year series gives a clear, numeric trail of how obligations moved from FY21 through FY26 to date.",
